.TH CYBERTODOPUNK 1 "October 2026" "cybertodopunk 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cybertodopunk \- meeting actions from the ACTIONS.tex files of LaTeX reports
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cybertodopunk
.br
.B cybertodopunk list
[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-company\fR \fIC\fR | \fB\-\-all\-companies\fR] [\fB\-\-everyone\fR] [\fB\-\-done\fR]
.br
.B cybertodopunk done
\fIFILE\fR \fIID\fR [\fB\-\-at\fR "\fIYYYY\-MM\-DD HH:MM\fR"]
.br
.B cybertodopunk start
|
.B reopen
\fIFILE\fR \fIID\fR
.br
.B cybertodopunk switch
\fICOMPANY\fR
.br
.B cybertodopunk config
[\fBshow\fR | \fBname\fR \fINAME\fR | \fBalias\fR|\fBpath\fR|\fBcompany\fR \fBadd\fR|\fBrm\fR \fIVALUE\fR | \fBteam on\fR|\fBoff\fR]
.br
.B cybertodopunk new
[\fIDIR\fR]
.br
.B cybertodopunk convert
\fIREPORT.tex\fR... [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-input\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.br
.B cybertodopunk check
[\fIDIR\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A meeting report folder is named \fIYYYYMMDD_COMPANY_subject\fR and holds an
\fBACTIONS.tex\fR that the report includes with \fB\\input{ACTIONS}\fR in its
action-plan section. Each action is one
\fB\\actionitem{\fIID\fB}{\fIOwner\fB}{\fIDue\fB}{\fIStatus\fB}{\fICompleted\fB}{\fIDescription\fB}\fR,
with status \fBtodo\fR, \fBinprogress\fR or \fBdone\fR.
.PP
Without arguments, the window opens. \fBlist\fR shows the open actions whose
owner contains the configured surname (the word in capitals of the full name,
else its last word) or an alias, for the active company. \fBdone\fR writes
the status and the completion time into ACTIONS.tex, so the next compilation
of the report shows them; \fBreopen\fR undoes it.
.PP
\fBconvert\fR moves the hand\-written action longtable of an older report into
a new ACTIONS.tex and replaces it with \fB\\input{ACTIONS}\fR.
\fBcheck\fR parses every ACTIONS.tex found and reports errors.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/cybertodopunk/config.json
Settings (\fBCYBERTODOPUNK_CONFIG\fR overrides the path).
.TP
.I /usr/share/cybertodopunk/latex/ACTIONS\-TEMPLATE.tex
The ACTIONS.tex template.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR metamonitor (1),
.BR latexmk (1)
